    "media:imagetext": "S•S. President Piezee,\nAugust 25, 1937.\nDear 1r. Morgan:\nMy long memo\nof aug. 18th was written in a zush and read\nover hurriedly in an attempt to catch the Hoover.\nMies Porbes\nmay have rewritten said memo at Manila and in so doing she\nmay have corrected some of the obvious mistakes.\nIn oalmly\nreviewing that memo heze on the peaceful Pierce, I note a\nfew typographical errors and one or two important factors\nwhich should be corrected.\nIn deseribing Pilot Sharp's experiences on the 14th the\nemo, as my temporary stenographer wrote it, reads - - \"a great\nof confusion during the course of which Allison telephoned\nfrom Lunghwa advising that Sharp upon arrival at Hankow found\nno one at the field ---\".\nThe memo should read upon arrival\nat lanchang\".\nMy memo under reference aleo failed to deseribe how the\nsecond Dolphin happened to return to shanghai.\nThe eiroun-\nstances were as follows:\nYou will remember that thursday\nairplanee to be away tzom lunghwa.\nAccordingly Conver\n(a new pilot who had been flying the Dolphins for ONAC under\ncharter) flew the polphin to Hanking tharsday Aag. 12 and\nstayed over night.\nThe next day, Friday aug. 13ch, he re-\nturned to Shanghai and, ilying the soheduled special service,\ncarried a full load of\npassengers to lanking and a full\nload from Wanking to Klukiang, from which latter point he\nreturned only as ter as lanking so as to keep the Dolphin\naway from shanghai.\non Saturday aug. 14th it became evident\nthat our american pilots at flanking were not reoeiving all\nmeasages sent to them, as evidenced by the Stinson t1ights\nof pilots rottsonidt and Sweet undertaken after 41lison\nhad wired them to remain in Manking for further instructions.\nAfter Sweet and Pottschmidt left Manking we had two pilots\nLeft there, namely Harry Smith and Conover.\nabout these men in view of what had happened to Sweet and\nPottsehmidt and acoordingly ordered Conover to piok up Harry\nSmith as a pessenger and ?1y to winghong (a point on the\n\"nampoo neas shangal) For some reason, not quite olear\nto me, Allison later ordered Conover to fly to shanghai\ninstead of Minghong and that is why we had both Dolphine\nat shanghai on londay Aug 16th.\nConover was checked out\nonly for the special CIAO charter Dolphin service between\nshanghai and Klukiang via Nanking and was of course not\nqualified to fly the Dolphin to longkong.\nMy memo of the 18th also failed to state that on aug.\nPilot leleon flew a so-called \"charter\" trip for which\nONAC received nothing but the thanke of the Minieter of Com-\nmunications, at whose instance the trip was made.\n\"charter\" trip was made in the DO-2 under the following\neiroumstances.\nThe Miniater of Communications, General\nordered Nelson to lanking for an undisclosed charter trip\nto an unannounced destination.\nAllison reminded the Managing\nDirector, through whom the order came, that lelson had had\nfer too much flying and should have a rest,\nbut finally\napproved the trip on aseurances that it would be just a",
